cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use T2GD in work you publish, please cite it as below."
title: "T2GD: transcriptome-space to genome-space BAM conversion toolkit"
abstract: >-
  T2GD converts alignments made against a transcriptome FASTA into genome
  coordinates, using a GTF annotation as the map. Each transcript-space
  alignment is lifted onto the genome, its CIGAR split at every exon
  boundary it crosses, and an N operation inserted for each intron, so the
  converted record is a spliced genomic alignment that genome browsers,
  variant callers and coverage tools read correctly. The toolkit provides
  36 subcommands around that core operation, covering inspection,
  filtering, sorting, indexing, counting, splice-junction cataloguing,
  plotting and validation. It ships as two dependency-free executables, a
  desktop application and a command line tool, the latter carrying no
  graphical code at all so that it runs on cluster nodes and in containers.
type: software
version: 1.19.1
date-released: "2026-08-09"
license: CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0
# Concept DOI, not the version DOI.  Zenodo mints the version DOI when the
# release is published, so it cannot be written here beforehand; carrying
# 1.19.0's would point every citation of 1.19.1 at the wrong snapshot.  The
# concept DOI always resolves to the latest version and is correct at all
# times.  Add the 1.19.1 snapshot DOI to `identifiers` once Zenodo issues it.
